From beff6a430588278e7fa3e6cb0c87db26f779d812 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:53:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: camss: validate formats on every CSID source pad

CSID exposes four source pads and propagates sink formats to all of
them. However, csid_try_format() handles only the first source pad.
S_FMT on pads 2 through 4 consequently accepts arbitrary codes and
dimensions, and frame-size enumeration does not use the sink format.

Handle all source pads with the existing source-format logic. With
the test generator disabled, derive their formats from the sink and
the backend's supported output codes. Keep test-generator validation
consistent on every source pad.

This also covers the SM8750 IPP path on source pad 4 without changing
the image capture format or adding a private interface.
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid.c
index 48459b46a..b55cf8a9b 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid.c
@@ -843,6 +843,9 @@ static void csid_try_format(struct csid_device *csid,
 		break;
 
 	case MSM_CSID_PAD_SRC:
+	case MSM_CSID_PAD_SRC + 1:
+	case MSM_CSID_PAD_SRC + 2:
+	case MSM_CSID_PAD_SRC + 3:
 		if (csid->testgen.nmodes == CSID_PAYLOAD_MODE_DISABLED ||
 		    csid->testgen_mode->cur.val == 0) {
 			/* Test generator is disabled, */
-- 
